      a device check.
CAVEAT:  Each level-1 reset erased flash and reset the level (STEPs 2-8: `sho boot` image
  Not set, config file not found, Security Level none). The Test Engineer ruled the
  difference between the script's expected 'Erasing flash' and the device's "Erasing
  nand0:" a wording difference (2026-10-07); 2005.3-2005.8 accepted "Erasing nand0" through
  the patched library_5700.py.
  2005.7: the suite's timeout check sends no password at all and waits 60 s
  (selectBootMenuOptionPWTimeout(self, dut, 1, "", 60), test-5700.2005.py line 936), so it
  exercises the no-entry timeout (method step 4). There is no separate check for the
  partial-entry or valid-entry-without-Return timeouts (method steps 5-6), and the exact
  moment the prompt timed out is not measured: the check is that AW+ booted (`show boot`
  readable) after the 60 s wait.
  2005.8: the TestCase title says levels 2 & 3 stop access to Start-Shell; the suite's own
  check asserts "Start-Shell is accessible when in security level 2" and refused only at
  level 3, and the unit did exactly that.

